        "checkedAt": "2026-11-20T18:34:51.680Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E3",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "At Microsoft Ignite , the companies are expanding access to Azure virtual machines powered by NVIDIA Vera Rubin NVL72 systems, as well as adding customer availability to NVIDIA open models and customization capabilities through Microsoft Foundry, and new options for running AI…",
        "sourceUrl": "https://blogs.nvidia.com/blog/microsoft-ignite-accelerated-computing-azure-windows-pcs/",
        "source": "NVIDIA Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-19T20:00:15.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-20T18:34:51.680Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E4",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Microsoft is also using NVIDIA technologies to accelerate its own models and services, including NVIDIA Dynamo inference software for post-training and NVIDIA RTX PRO 6000 Blackwell GPUs for Bing search models.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://blogs.nvidia.com/blog/microsoft-ignite-accelerated-computing-azure-windows-pcs/",
