      },
      {
        "id": "E5",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "NVIDIA Vera Rubin NVL72 Running in Azure",
        "sourceUrl": "https://blogs.nvidia.com/blog/microsoft-ignite-accelerated-computing-azure-windows-pcs/",
        "source": "NVIDIA Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-19T20:00:15.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-20T18:34:51.680Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E6",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "NVIDIA Vera Rubin NVL72 systems are running in Azure data centers , providing infrastructure designed for demanding reasoning, agentic applications, and large-scale model training and inference.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://blogs.nvidia.com/blog/microsoft-ignite-accelerated-computing-azure-windows-pcs/",
        "source": "NVIDIA Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-19T20:00:15.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-20T18:34:51.680Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E7",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "To help data centers get more performance from available power, NVIDIA and Microsoft are also collaborating on power efficiency using NVIDIA MaxLPS .",
        "sourceUrl": "https://blogs.nvidia.com/blog/microsoft-ignite-accelerated-computing-azure-windows-pcs/",
        "source": "NVIDIA Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-19T20:00:15.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-20T18:34:51.680Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E8",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Azure’s Vera Rubin preview builds on NVIDIA and Microsoft’s codesign and performance optimization, underscored in the latest NVIDIA Blackwell-based MLPerf results.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://blogs.nvidia.com/blog/microsoft-ignite-accelerated-computing-azure-windows-pcs/",
        "source": "NVIDIA Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-19T20:00:15.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-20T18:34:51.680Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E9",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "On Windows PCs powered by NVIDIA RTX Spark , NVIDIA and Microsoft will showcase local large language model experiences at Ignite, demonstrating how developers can run AI applications directly on devices.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://blogs.nvidia.com/blog/microsoft-ignite-accelerated-computing-azure-windows-pcs/",
        "source": "NVIDIA Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-19T20:00:15.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-20T18:34:51.680Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E10",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "For organizations using Cloud PCs, the companies are bringing Direct Stream capabilities to GPU-accelerated Windows 365 Cloud PCs.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://blogs.nvidia.com/blog/microsoft-ignite-accelerated-computing-azure-windows-pcs/",
        "source": "NVIDIA Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-19T20:00:15.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-20T18:34:51.680Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E11",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Alongside expanding customer access to NVIDIA technologies, Microsoft is using NVIDIA software and accelerated computing in its own AI development and services.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://blogs.nvidia.com/blog/microsoft-ignite-accelerated-computing-azure-windows-pcs/",
        "source": "NVIDIA Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-19T20:00:15.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-20T18:34:51.680Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E12",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Visit NVIDIA at Ignite for demonstrations spanning enterprise applications, robotics, accelerated data processing and local computing, with hardware including an NVIDIA GB300 NVL72 rack and RTX Spark devices.",
